      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Cardiac disease is a leading cause of disability. This article reviews the epidemiology, pathophysiology, and risk factors for coronary heart disease. We explore the latest research in risk stratification, exercise training, and screening for cardiac rehabilitation in the elderly patient. The rehabilitation specialist will see how this select population differs in their medical and rehabilitative needs."},
